---
/**
 * Programs (/ngo/program) — NGO "Our Programs". Built against Figma node 7447:6027
 * ("PROGRAM PAGE NGO" — confirmed by frame name, no collision to resolve unlike About/Partners).
 *
 * ⚠ REDESIGNED 2026-08-07, the same sweep that reworked About. The page was first built
 * (Phase 4, docs/ngo-build-plan.md) against the 2026-07-20 ingest, which is what
 * design/figma/…/7447-6027/node.json still holds. That snapshot is STALE — it is 4593px tall
 * where the live frame is 4264px. This build follows the LIVE node, read through the Figma MCP;
 * every value below was confirmed against it, not against the committed node.json. Re-run
 * `npm run figma:fetch` (needs FIGMA_API_KEY) to resync. What changed, and is now reflected here:
 *   - A full-bleed photo hero + "Our Programs" h1 replaced the white "HOME / PROGRAMS"
 *     breadcrumb header. The breadcrumb is gone from the design entirely, exactly as on About.
 *   - The whole "Partner Programs" block — centred intro plus three deep-teal cards (the old
 *     node 7447:6518) — was deleted. The design now runs GVP straight into "Contact Us Now"
 *     with nothing between them, and offers no replacement section.
 *   - The three detail photos are re-cropped, mirrored and square-cornered (see below).
 *
 * The page is now four blocks: the hero, three program-detail sections, and the contact panel.
 *
 *   1. Photo hero — `SubPageHero`, the same component Consultancy's seven sub-pages and NGO
 *      About use. The redesign gave Program the identical 1440×670 / 25%-scrim / bottom-120 /
 *      `u-page-title` treatment, and its photo is byte-identical to About's (RMSE 0), so it
 *      takes the shared `ngoHeroPhoto` rather than a second copy of anything.
 *   2. The program-detail sections (node 7447:6030 vertical stack, 120px itemSpacing) —
 *      alternating photo/copy: the design's THREE are STEP (photo left), HEALS (photo right),
 *      GVP (photo left), and they are **CMS-driven as of 2026-08-15** (`@lib/programs`, the same
 *      published list Home's card grid takes its first four from; the design's three are that
 *      module's fixtures, so a fixture build renders this frame unchanged). A configured-but-
 *      empty CMS renders none of them, leaving the hero above the contact panel — the same
 *      "empty states are real" call the Resources listing makes, and not one the fixtures can
 *      reach. Each is
 *      a 40px `u-h3` heading + the same placeholder GIEVA paragraph + a tinted green "Learn more
 *      about us" button (`Button variant="secondary"` — the design's `GIEVA Button` here is
 *      `bg rgba(0,127,14,.05)` / `border rgba(0,127,14,.1)` / 8px radius / 33×17 padding / 16px
 *      label→arrow gap / 20px arrow, which is that variant exactly).
 *   3. "Contact Us Now" — the deep-teal inverse form panel (node 7447:6444), UNCHANGED by the
 *      redesign. Structurally the SAME 7-field labelled `<form>` as the NGO Partners "Become a
 *      Partner" panel (fixed 387px right-aligned label column, 122px gap, white-underline
 *      inputs, centred submit) — but its labels are a MUTED teal-blue #69A4B8 (node fill), NOT
 *      Partners' green #007F0E, and its heading accent ("Now") is green. All seven visible
 *      labels read "What is your name?" in the source (placeholder/duplicated design copy) —
 *      reproduced verbatim per exact-replica-first, each wired to a uniquely-id'd input so the
 *      label→input association stays valid.
 *
 * GEOMETRY RECONCILES, so the reading above is verified rather than eyeballed: hero 670 + body
 * 2970 = Main 3640; body = 120 + 450 + 120 + 450 + 120 + 450 + 120 + 1020 + 120 = 2970; and one
 * detail column = 40 + 92 + 40 + (120 + 64 + 54) + 40 = 450, the measured row height.
 *
 * TYPE: "Contact Us Now" keeps `u-section-title`. Do NOT "fix" it to `u-h2` by analogy with
 * About — About moved because *its* headings specify tracking −0.26, whereas this frame's h2
 * (node 7447:6448) really does carry −3.3px, which is what `u-section-title` resolves to.
 *
 * Heading order: h1 "Our Programs" → h2 STEP → h2 HEALS → h2 GVP → h2 "Contact Us Now". No level
 * is skipped.
 *
 * Tracked colour-contrast gaps (docs/a11y-known-issues.md N14–N15, allowlisted with Program-only
 * parent classes in tests/a11y.spec.ts): the green "Now" accent (2.27:1 on teal) and the muted
 * #69A4B8 form labels (4.27:1 on teal) — both confirmed source-design colours, shipped as
 * designed per CLAUDE.md #2. N12 (the orange breadcrumb) and N13 (the green Partner-Programs
 * "Learn more" links) retired with the markup that carried them. Everything structural
 * (landmarks, heading order, keyboard, focus, reduced-motion) passes clean.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '@components/Button.astro';
import SubPageHero from '@components/SubPageHero.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { ngoHeroPhoto } from '@lib/ngo-hero-images';
import { programPhoto } from '@lib/ngo-program-images';
import { getProgramDetails } from '@lib/programs';

/**
 * The program-detail sections — CMS-driven as of 2026-08-15 (`@lib/programs`), from the same
 * published list Home's card grid takes its first four from. The design's own three live on as
 * that module's detail fixtures, so a build with no `GIEVA_API_URL` renders this page exactly as
 * the frame does. Rendered in the API's own order (`order ASC`), all of them: this is the page
 * every programme is entitled to a section on, and it is where Home's `#slug` links land.
 *
 * Three things the CMS does NOT supply, and why they stay here:
 *
 * - **The photo/copy alternation.** The design runs photo-left, photo-right, photo-left
 *   (node 7447:6415 is the mirrored one), which is a rhythm of the layout rather than a property
 *   of a programme, so it is computed from the index. On the three fixtures that reproduces the
 *   frame exactly, and it keeps alternating for however many the client publishes.
 * - **The "Learn more about us" destination.** No model field could hold it. Every one of these
 *   buttons used to point at `/ngo/program`, i.e. the page rendering them, so all three were
 *   no-ops; the label the design sets is "Learn more about us" and `/ngo/about` is what that
 *   sentence names. If the client ever wants per-programme pages, `GET /api/programs/all/:slug`
 *   is already there to back a `/ngo/program/[slug]` route and this becomes that link instead.
 * - **The section `id`.** It is the CMS `slug` now rather than a hand-written acronym — the same
 *   value Home builds its anchors from, so the two can no longer drift apart.
 */
const details = await getProgramDetails();

// The design's own label on all three buttons (node 7463:5844) — see above for why it is here.
const detailHref = '/ngo/about';

// Seven contact fields — all labelled "What is your name?" in the source (node 7447:6451),
// reproduced verbatim; unique ids keep each label→input association valid.
const contactFields = Array.from({ length: 7 }, (_, i) => ({
  id: `contact-${i + 1}`,
  label: 'What is your name?',
}));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Programs — GIEVA NGO"
  description="GIEVA's flagship programs — STEP, HEALS, and the GIEVA Volunteer Project — transforming young lives across Nigeria."
  brand="ngo"
>
  <!-- ── Photo hero (node 12330:13420) ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <SubPageHero title="Our Programs" photo={ngoHeroPhoto} />

  <div class="container program">
    <!-- ── Program detail sections (STEP / HEALS / GVP) ───────────────────────── -->
    {
      details.map((detail, i) => (
        <section
          class="program__detail"
          id={detail.slug || undefined}
          data-reversed={i % 2 === 1 ? '' : undefined}
        >
          {/* A programme's own hero photo when the CMS has one, else the design's placeholder.
              `heroImageUrl` is a remote Cloudinary URL, which `astro:assets` cannot process
              without `image.remotePatterns` in astro.config.mjs — and that host is not confirmed
              yet — so it renders as a plain <img> with explicit dimensions and `loading="lazy"`:
              correct and CLS-free, just unoptimised. Same call, and the same one-line reversal
              once the CDN host is known, as `ArticleCard.astro` and `TeamCard.astro`.

              `alt=""` either way. The design's placeholder is decorative, and a real photo has no
              alt-text field in the model — the only candidates are the empty string or the
              programme title, which the heading immediately beside it already states. Logged
              with the other Program asks in docs/backend-api-requests.md.

              `data-remote` marks the CMS branch, NOT the placeholder one, so the placeholder's
              markup stays byte-identical to the pre-integration page. It turns off the two
              treatments that belong to the design's own fill rather than to any photo — see the
              CSS. */}
          {detail.imageUrl ? (
            <img
              class="program__detail-media"
              src={detail.imageUrl}
              alt=""
              width={636}
              height={450}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              data-remote
            />
          ) : (
            <Image
              src={programPhoto}
              alt=""
              width={636}
              height={450}
              class="program__detail-media"
            />
          )}
          <div class="program__detail-body">
            <h2 class="u-h3 program__detail-title">{detail.title}</h2>
            <div class="program__detail-copy">
              {detail.description && (
                <p class="u-body-lg program__detail-desc">{detail.description}</p>
              )}
              <Button variant="secondary" href={detailHref}>
                Learn more about us
              </Button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <!-- ── Contact Us Now ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="program-contact surface-inverse" id="contact-form" data-surface="inverse">
      <div class="program-contact__header">
        <h2 class="u-section-title">
          Contact Us <em class="u-accent-em">Now</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="u-body-lg">
          Answer Interview questions to help us know how we can impact lives together
        </p>
      </div>

      <form class="program-contact__body">
        <div class="program-contact__fields">
          {
            contactFields.map((field) => (
              <>
                <label class="program-contact__label u-body-lg" for={field.id}>
                  {field.label}
                </label>
                <div class="program-contact__control">
                  <input
                    id={field.id}
                    class="program-contact__input u-body-lg"
                    type="text"
                    name={field.id}
                    placeholder="Your Answer"
                    required
                  />
                </div>
              </>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <div class="program-contact__submit">
          <Button variant="primary" type="submit">Send Message</Button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Page flow ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The body below the hero is node 7447:6030: 120px padding top and bottom, and 120px
     between blocks (--space-6xl, matching itemSpacing). The top padding used to exist to
     clear the old in-flow page header; post-redesign it is simply the node's own padding. */
  .program {
    display: grid;
    padding-top: var(--space-6xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6xl);
    row-gap: var(--space-6xl);
  }

  /* ── Program detail sections ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
     node 7463:5838 etc.: HORIZONTAL, two equal 636px columns with a 40px gap, both columns
     `self-stretch`. `data-reversed` swaps the photo to the right for HEALS (node 7447:6415). */
  .program__detail {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    /* Anchor targets (#step / #heals / #gvp) for Home's program cards — see the `details` array.
       The offset that keeps them clear of the sticky masthead is global: `scroll-padding-top` on
       <html> in base.css. */
  }
  .program__detail[data-reversed] .program__detail-media {
    order: 2;
  }
  /* The photo is SQUARE-cornered in the design — no radius on node 7463:5840, confirmed by
     cropping the rendered node's corners, not by reading the layer name ("rounded-rectangle"
     is just Figma's node type). It is also MIRRORED: the fill carries `scaleX(-1)`, which puts
     the plant on the left of the frame. The mirror lives here rather than baked into the asset
     so the committed file stays the unmodified Figma export. `object-position: bottom` is the
     node's own fill alignment; the crop itself is baked into the asset (see @lib/
     ngo-program-images for why the raw imageRef export is the wrong file to use). */
  .program__detail-media {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: bottom;
    transform: scaleX(-1);
    display: block;
  }
  /* Both of those last two belong to the design's placeholder FILL, not to "a programme photo":
     the mirror is that fill's `scaleX(-1)` and the bottom alignment is its own crop origin.
     Applying either to a photo the client uploaded would flip their image left-for-right and
     crop it from an origin nobody chose, so the CMS branch opts out. (Scoped this way round —
     the override on the remote image rather than the rules on the placeholder — so the
     placeholder's markup and CSS stay exactly what they were before the CMS integration.) */
  .program__detail-media[data-remote] {
    object-position: center;
    transform: none;
  }
  /* Copy column (node 7463:5841): 40px block padding, then a 40px gap from the heading to the
     copy block — which itself puts 64px between the paragraph and the button (node 7463:5844
     itemSpacing 64, NOT the 40 above it). Those two gaps differ in the design; don't collapse
     them into one. */
  .program__detail-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .program__detail-copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  .program__detail-title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-default); /* violet #120633 */
  }
  .program__detail-desc {
    margin: 0;
    color: #000; /* node fill #000000 on the body copy */
  }

  /* ── Contact Us Now ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     node 7447:6444: deep-teal inverse panel (#0E3E40), 12px radius, 64px padding + 64px gap
     between header / fields / submit. Same labelled-form shape as the NGO Partners panel, but
     the labels are a MUTED teal-blue #69A4B8 here (node fill), not Partners' green, and the
     accent is green ("Now"). Untouched by the 2026-08 redesign. */
  .program-contact {
    padding: var(--space-3xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  .program-contact__header {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    justify-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .program-contact__header h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .program-contact__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  /* Fixed 387px label column, RIGHT-aligned text, 122px gap to a filling input (node: Label
     sizingH FIXED w=387, row itemSpacing 122) — the same one-off values as the NGO Partners
     form. Rows are 16px apart (node itemSpacing 16).

     Each row is a FIXED 74px, which is taller than its own content: the input box is only 42px
     of it (node 7447:6456) and the remaining 32px is empty. Letting the rows size to content
     instead — which is what they did until 2026-08-07 — collapses each one to 42px and the
     whole panel to 796px against the frame's measured 1020px. The arithmetic is
     7 × 74 + 6 × 16 = 614, which is the measured height of node 7447:6451 exactly, and
     64 + 96 + 64 + 614 + 64 + 54 + 64 = 1020, the panel. Top-align, or the 32px splits itself
     around the input and the underline drifts off the design's baseline. */
  .program-contact__fields {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 387px minmax(0, 1fr);
    column-gap: 122px;
    row-gap: var(--space-sm);
    grid-auto-rows: 74px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  /* Muted teal-blue labels #69A4B8 (node fill) — distinct from Partners' green labels.
     The 8px offset is the label text's y within its own 74px row cell (node 7447:6454), which
     lines its baseline up with the input's text rather than with the top of the input box. */
  .program-contact__label {
    color: #69a4b8;
    text-align: right;
    padding-top: var(--space-2xs);
  }
  .program-contact__control {
    display: flex;
  }
  .program-contact__input {
    width: 100%;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-white);
    padding-block: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--color-text-inverse);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
  }
  .program-contact__input::placeholder {
    color: var(--color-text-inverse);
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .program-contact__input:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--color-focus-ring);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  /* Submit centred in the panel (node: GIEVA Button counterAxisAlignItems CENTER). */
  .program-contact__submit {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     No tablet/mobile NGO Program frame exists in the design; these are our authored,
     content-preserving reflows (same approach as the other NGO pages). */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .program-contact__fields {
      grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr);
      column-gap: var(--space-3xl);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .program__detail {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-lg);
    }
    /* Stacked, the row no longer has a copy column to take its height from, so the photo goes
       back to carrying the design's own 636×450 ratio. */
    .program__detail-media {
      height: auto;
      aspect-ratio: 636 / 450;
    }
    .program__detail-body {
      padding-block: 0;
    }
    /* Keep the photo above the copy on every stacked section for a consistent reading order. */
    .program__detail[data-reversed] .program__detail-media {
      order: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    /* Panel padding drops 64→32 so the 48px heading isn't squeezed on a 375px viewport. */
    .program-contact {
      padding: var(--space-lg);
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
    }
    .program-contact__body {
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
    }
    /* Stacked, the fixed 74px row is meaningless — label and input become their own rows, so
       they go back to sizing to content. */
    .program-contact__fields {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-auto-rows: auto;
      row-gap: var(--space-3xs);
    }
    .program-contact__label {
      text-align: left;
      padding-top: 0;
      margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    }
  }
</style>
